        "comments": "The assembly mSciVul1.2 is based on 23x PacBio data and 44x 10X Genomics Chromium data generated at the Wellcome Sanger Institute, BioNano data generated at the Rockefeller University Vertebrate Genome Laboratory, and 17x Hi-C data generated at the Baylor College of Medicine. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Falcon-unzip, retained haplotig identification with purge_dups, 10X based scaffolding with scaff10x, BioNano hybrid-scaffolding, Hi-C based scaffolding and improvement by the Aiden lab as part of a collaboration with DNA Zoo using 3D-DNA and Juicebox, Arrow polishing, and two rounds of FreeBayes polishing. The mitochondrial assembly was produced at The Rockefeller University using mitoVGP. Finally, the assembly was analysed and manually improved using gEVAL. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size.\n\nStructural annotation is propagated from INSDC submissions or other annotation providers and processed to follow RefSeq standards. Functional annotation is provided by RefSeq, and is derived from model organism databases, orthologous species, curation, domain architecture analysis, and submitted information.",
